# =====================================================================
#  What is in this repository: the source, the tests and the docs.
#  What is not: anything a build regenerates, and the raw 3D exports.
# =====================================================================

# ---- generated: rebuild with ./build.sh, never commit ----
# A tracked build is how the shipped file silently went four versions stale
# once already. Both of these come out of `node tools/build.js`, and the
# single-file build is published as a release asset instead.
dev.html
R2D2-Simulator.html
# pca-studio/PCA-Studio.html is ALSO generated by the same ./build.sh, and is
# deliberately TRACKED: it is 250 KB rather than 7 MB, and the whole promise
# of that folder is "open this one file from disk", which a clone should keep
# without needing a build first. ./test.sh runs against it, so a stale one
# fails loudly rather than silently.
docs/shots/shot-*.png

# ---- dependencies ----
node_modules/

# ---- scratch ----
tmp/
_stage/
_to_delete/
.codex_tmp/
*.log
.DS_Store

# ---- the working folder's local-only corners ----
# `_local-assets/` is the raw material the repository deliberately does not
# carry: MrBaddeley's OBJ exports, the STEP, the Padawan sound pack, the .r2m
# intermediates and Pololu's manual. It sits beside the source so the CAD
# pipeline can be re-run; it must never be committed. `output/` is renders,
# posters and video — big, generated, and nobody else needs them.
_local-assets/
output/
R2.old/

# =====================================================================
#  RAW 3D SOURCE — LOCAL ONLY, DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
#
#  The MK4 and Polar Mouse OBJ exports are MrBaddeley's paid Patreon
#  models. The rigged, decimated `payload.js` that this simulator loads is
#  included with his permission (see CREDITS.md); the raw exports are not,
#  and never have been. They are also 250 MB, and GitHub rejects anything
#  over 100 MB.
#
#  You only need them to RE-RIG from scratch with cad/convert.py or
#  cad/mouse.py — which needs the models, which you get from him.
# =====================================================================
*.obj
*.mtl
*.step
*.stl
*.mp4

# ---- the sound pack: 18 MB of MP3s that are not ours to ship ----
# Drop the Padawan sound-pack zip onto the running app instead; it keeps it
# in your own browser. See CREDITS.md.
Padawan_sounds_*.zip
